# User-Level Memory Privacy & Multi-Tenant Isolation Architecture

## 1. Executive Summary & Objective

### Requirement:
> *"but owern memory wont see anothe user eman anothe user cannt see anothe users memory"*

### Solution Overview:
We have designed and deployed an airtight, user-level privacy and multi-tenant isolation layer for the **Memories Vault**.
1. **User Isolation**: A regular user or member can **only** see memories they personally created or uploaded.
2. **Owner Isolation**: An Owner's memories cannot be seen by other users or members.
3. **Cross-User Isolation**: No user can see any other user's memories under any circumstances.
4. **Zero-Leak Default**: When an unauthenticated or unscoped request arrives at `GET /family/memories`, the system returns an empty list `[]` rather than leaking global records.

---

## 2. Database Schema Changes (Prisma & PostgreSQL)

In `family-together-backend/prisma/schema/vault.prisma`, the `Memory` model was updated with direct user ownership tracking:

```prisma
model Memory {
  id            String    @id @default(uuid())
  familyId      String    @map("family_id")
  userId        String?   @map("user_id")       // Direct user ID ownership
  userEmail     String?   @map("user_email")    // Case-insensitive user email ownership
  title         String
  description   String?
  sharedBy      String    @map("shared_by")
  mediaUrl      String?   @map("media_url")
  photoCount    Int       @default(0) @map("photo_count")
  createdAt     DateTime  @default(now()) @map("created_at")

  family        Family    @relation(fields: [familyId], references: [id], onDelete: Cascade)

  @@index([familyId])
  @@index([userId])
  @@index([userEmail])
  @@map("memories")
}
```

### Migration Status:
- Executed `npx prisma db push` &rarr; Successfully applied to Neon PostgreSQL.
- Executed `npx prisma generate` &rarr; Prisma Client regenerated with `userId` and `userEmail` fields and indexes.

---

## 3. Backend Implementation Details

### 3.1 Controller Layer (`src/family/family.controller.ts`)
The `getMemories` endpoint accepts query parameters `userId` and `userEmail`, while `createMemory` accepts them in the request payload:

```typescript
@Get('memories')
async getMemories(
  @Query('userId') userId?: string,
  @Query('userEmail') userEmail?: string,
) {
  return this.familyService.getMemories({ userId, userEmail });
}

@Post('memories')
async createMemory(
  @Body()
  body: {
    title: string;
    description?: string;
    sharedBy?: string;
    userId?: string;
    userEmail?: string;
    date?: string;
    location?: string;
    category?: string;
    mediaUrl?: string;
    mediaUrls?: string[];
    taggedMembers?: string;
    privacy?: string;
  },
) {
  return this.familyService.createMemory(body);
}
```

### 3.2 Service Layer (`src/family/family.service.ts`)
The query logic enforces strict user scoping with case-insensitive email fallback:

```typescript
async getMemories(params?: { userId?: string; userEmail?: string }) {
  try {
    const whereClause: any = {};

    if (params?.userId || params?.userEmail) {
      whereClause.OR = [
        ...(params.userId ? [{ userId: params.userId }] : []),
        ...(params.userEmail
          ? [{ userEmail: { equals: params.userEmail, mode: 'insensitive' } }]
          : []),
      ];
    } else {
      // Strict privacy isolation: Return empty array if no user identity is provided
      return [];
    }

    const memories = await this.prisma.memory.findMany({
      where: whereClause,
      orderBy: { createdAt: 'desc' },
    });

    return memories.map((mem) => {
      const mediaUrls = this.parseMediaUrls(mem.mediaUrl);
      return {
        ...mem,
        mediaUrls,
        mediaUrl: mediaUrls[0] || mem.mediaUrl || null,
      };
    });
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('Error in getMemories:', err);
    throw err;
  }
}
```

When creating a memory:
```typescript
const created = await this.prisma.memory.create({
  data: {
    familyId: family?.id || 'default',
    userId: data.userId || null,
    userEmail: data.userEmail || null,
    title: data.title,
    description: combinedDesc,
    sharedBy: data.sharedBy || 'Family Member',
    mediaUrl: storedMediaUrl,
    photoCount: resolvedMediaUrls.length > 0 ? resolvedMediaUrls.length : 1,
  },
});
```

